The board calculation at $00{:}49{:}35$ begins the entry-by-entry multiplication. Completing the products gives $\begin{aligned}
\sigma_{z}\sigma_{x}
&=
\begin{pmatrix}
0&1\\
-1&0
\end{pmatrix}
=i\sigma_{y},\\
\sigma_{x}\sigma_{z}
&=
\begin{pmatrix}
0&-1\\
1&0
\end{pmatrix}
=-i\sigma_{y}.\end{aligned}$ Hence $=2i\sigma_{y}.$ The extra factor of two is removed by defining the physical spin operators as $S_{i}=\frac{\hbar}{2}\sigma_{i}.$ Then $=i\hbar S_{y},$ and similarly for cyclic permutations. Half the Pauli matrices, with the factor of $\hbar$ restored, therefore form an angular-momentum system.

